exually assault someone essentially for  a joke it's south park i get that it's a  joke but that doesn't there's no like  part of a government guideline that says  unless it's a joke so that had to be  taken out  and i actually think that what they  replaced it with is much funnier  instead in the australian version  instead of what they considered to be  interactive sexual assault it's  it's this picture of a koala  crying  while a didgeridoo plays in the  background and there's text on screen  that's like wow australia we had to cut  this because of your government  censorship  which again i found to be significantly  funnier than the press button to anal  pro brandy neil valley said how do game  review codes work at a big company like  ign does ign have a steam account that  everyone plays games from or do you add  the game to your personal account if  it's your personal account you get to  keep the game  so  it depended on like the publisher and  the relationship that you had with them  like i had some publishers who would  just give me codes directly and then  yeah i would add them to a personal  account  which is obviously what happens for me  now ign does not have a shared steam  account um  actually funhouse had a  shared  steam account where every single game  was unlockable for free which is nuts  like i guess it was like this old  system that they had maybe from  machinima or something where every  single game  you could just get on steam  for free i'm pretty sure that's how it  worked at least it was nuts like so of  course we were all using that account to  buy things because  everything was there  it was amazing unfortunately a certain  employee  took it with them and changed the  password when they were removed from the  company which is a real dick move it's a  really shitty thing to do to all the  people who work there who like needed  that account to make content but ign  never had one of those so no it was that  publishers would allocate like a certain  amount of keys they would have available  and then it was usually given to the  people who were  on podcasts or needed it for news always  wikis the wikis would always get codes  and then yeah you'd add it to your  personal account and yes you would you  would keep it the code the game wouldn't  remove itself from your account  but  it's was always used for work they  wouldn't give you a code if you didn't  have some outlet to speak about  the thing or benefit the company it  wasn't like you were just getting  games to play for fun in your spare time  i mean you were but there was an  expectation that if you got a code you  would make content with the code unless  there was like such a huge excess of  them that that didn't apply rassy  shackle but said hi alana do you think  living on the west coast has made it  easier to get a video game writing job  also do you think game studios lean more  towards office work rather than working  from home  um  i mean i very intentionally moved to the  west coast of the united states from  australia so that i could get jobs in  the games industry i did that on purpose  like i moved when i was  21 and had  not enough money to even buy a mattress  i had nothing but i did it so that i  could be where the industry was for the  highest chances of being employed  and obviously that's why i stay so do i  think that's that's made it easier  definitely yes but um it's not like i  lived on the west coast first i moved to  the west coast  to be able to get those jobs do i think  game studios lean more towards office  work rather than working from home uh  would depend on the game studio but um  my stance  personally going forward because of a  number of like just health issues that i  have that are so much more manageable  now that i have a little bit more  freedom is that i will straight up never  go back to working in an office  full-time i will not do it  i would pass on a job that would ask me  to do that and obviously that's like a  super  privileged position that i'm in to be  able to do that but i know that i need  it for my own health  the last time i was working in an office  full-time i was fainting on a frequent  basis i was so unwell i was like a husk  of a human and not having to be in an  office all the time has meant that i  could just do a much better job of  looking after myself so  my health is the best it's been in a  really long time um so that's definitely  my stance and there are a lot of games  that uh  work with people who aren't even in the  same country where writing's concerned  it would be difficult to be like on the  writing team you know treated full time  but you can get writing assignments  contract that um would just straight up  be sent to you and then you just send it  back and those they do those  internationally so it's definitely not  impossible but to directly answer your  question you know i moved to california  to work in the games industry because i  knew that it would  make it easier  and it did  i think  [Music]  that is it from me today everyone thank  you all so much for watching  thank you to keep sponsoring the video  and i will see you guys next time  [Music]
 

